From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:02:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 090/147] hjviewer: the same words everywhere (UX-W1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U27: one table for the password-less states. The feature is "비밀번호 없는
연결" everywhere; Settings → Account says "내 계정에 등록됨", "비밀번호 없는
연결 켜짐(로그인한 기기 3대)", "서버와 동기화 안 됨", "다시 로그인 필요(보안 키
바뀜)", and the admin view the same words. A card of My PCs builds its second
line from hjv-api's `hjv` in the app's language (hjvPeerNote, kept per PC ID
from the device list in group_model.dart) once hjv-api sends `wake`; until
then, and for any note the server did not send with that `hjv`, the server's
note shows as it came.

U28: the About ID on the desktop and the phone, and the remote restart's
question, show the ID as "123 456 789"; the question is "다시 시작할까요?" /
"Restart this device?"; the account handle has no space before its
parenthesis; ko.rs "연결하는 중…", "로그인하는 중…". (The card menu's "연결
<ID>" is plain "연결" in an account build since 1.8.2.)

U31: the login dialog's block says which password goes in: "연세포탈 ID와
연세포탈 비밀번호로 로그인합니다. 이용 비밀번호는 여기에 넣지 않습니다." The
pilot notice is on the About screen only, reworded for a service that is for
faculty and staff as a whole.

U32: one verb for logging another device out: [로그아웃], [내가 아님], "…
로그아웃했습니다", "…에서 로그아웃함"; the quoted button name holds a no-break
space so that a phone does not break it.

U34 (D-17): About says who "관리자" is: "HJViewer 관리자: <contact>", the
contact of the signed version policy (contact_ko) as the update model holds
it, else the maker; never a contact in the app. The admin view says "관리자
화면", "관리자 기록"; English "Made by ProjectTF".

U35: English says "faculty and staff" (A1, G3, L1-L4, the offline and
restart lines, the logout of other devices) and "a faculty or staff
member" (P3); "not synced with the server", "has not reported how to wake
it". The Korean stays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
